+# hive-bin (AUR)
+
+Prebuilt [Hive](https://github.com/ivankuznetsov/hive) binary for Arch Linux —
+a folder-as-agent pipeline driving an eight-stage multi-agent workflow from a
+TUI or your coding agent. This package ships the **self-contained,
+vendored-Ruby binary** from GitHub Releases (no system Ruby, no build step).
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+git clone https://aur.archlinux.org/hive-bin.git
+cd hive-bin
+makepkg -si
+```
+
+Or via an AUR helper:
+
+```bash
+yay -S hive-bin
+```
+
+Verify:
+
+```bash
+hive --version
+```
+
+If a foreign `hive` (e.g. Apache Hive) already owns the name, this package
+also installs the conflict-safe `hv` alias:
+
+```bash
+hv --version
+```
+
+## Upgrade / remove
+
+```bash
+yay -Syu hive-bin     # upgrade (also what `hive update` shells out to)
+yay -R hive-bin       # remove
+```
+
+## Notes
+
+- The package is **always named `hive-bin`** regardless of binary conflict
+  resolution.
+- `hive-git` (build-from-source) is deferred.
+- The `sha256sums` pin is the U1 release checksum; update `pkgver` and
+  `sha256sums` together on each release.
diff --git a/packaging/build.sh b/packaging/build.sh
new file mode 100755
index 000000000..1ff42f905
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packaging/build.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# Build the self-contained hive binary for one tier-1 target via Tebako
+# (plan: install/packaging U1). Produces dist/<target>/hive plus a verification
+# report. Run from the repo root:
+#
+#   TEBAKO_TARGET=hive-macos-arm64 ./packaging/build.sh
+#
+# The Charm FFI shared libraries (bubbletea / lipgloss) are the one piece
+# Tebako does not trivially bundle (plan Risks R1). This script verifies they
+# were captured and, if not, emits the documented fallback notice rather than
+# silently shipping a TUI-broken binary.
+set -euo pipefail
+
+TARGET="${1:-${TEBAKO_TARGET:-hive-linux-x86_64-glibc}}"
+DIST_DIR="dist/${TARGET}"
+OUT_BIN="${DIST_DIR}/hive"
+
+mkdir -p "${DIST_DIR}"
+
+if command -v tebako >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+  tebako package \
+    --config packaging/tebako.yml \
+    --output "${OUT_BIN}"
+elif [ -x ./bin/tebako ]; then
+  ./bin/tebako package --config packaging/tebako.yml --output "${OUT_BIN}"
+else
+  echo "tebako: not found on PATH and ./bin/tebako missing" >&2
+  echo "install tebako (https://github.com/tamatebako/tebako) or run the release CI job" >&2
+  exit 1
+fi
+
+chmod +x "${OUT_BIN}"
+
+# --- R1 verification: are the Charm FFI shared libraries captured? ----------
+# A vendored binary that can't load bubbletea/lipgloss still runs every
+# headless verb; only the TUI path breaks. Detect that and surface the
+# fallback instead of failing the whole build silently.
+#
+# The Tebako binary's entrypoint is the hive CLI (not a `ruby` subcommand), so
+# the check must use a real entrypoint: `hive ffi-check` requires bubbletea +
+# lipgloss and prints `ffi-ok` iff both load.
+VERIFY_REPORT="${DIST_DIR}/ffi-verification.txt"
+if "${OUT_BIN}" ffi-check > "${VERIFY_REPORT}" 2>&1; then
+  echo "ffi: charm libraries captured (TUI path OK)"
+else
+  {
+    echo "ffi: WARNING — Charm FFI shared libraries were NOT captured into the binary."
+    echo "     The TUI path (hive tui) will not work without system Ruby/gems."
+    echo "     See plan Risks R1 for the documented fallback chain."
+  } >> "${VERIFY_REPORT}"
+  cat "${VERIFY_REPORT}" >&2
+fi
+
+echo "built ${OUT_BIN}"
+echo "verification report: ${VERIFY_REPORT}"
