+# homebrew-hive
+
+Homebrew tap for [Hive](https://github.com/ivankuznetsov/hive) — a
+folder-as-agent pipeline that drives an eight-stage multi-agent workflow
+(`1-inbox` → `2-brainstorm` → `3-plan` → `4-execute` → `5-open-pr` →
+`6-review` → `7-finalize` → `8-done`) from a TUI or your coding agent.
+
+The formula installs the **self-contained, vendored-Ruby binary** published on
+GitHub Releases — no system Ruby, no build step.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+brew tap <org>/homebrew-hive
+brew install hive
+hive --version
+```
+
+If a foreign `hive` (e.g. Apache Hive) already owns the name, use the
+conflict-safe `hv` alias this formula also installs:
+
+```bash
+hv --version
+```
+
+## Upgrade / remove
+
+```bash
+brew upgrade hive
+brew uninstall hive
+```
+
+`hive update` shells out to `brew upgrade hive` (it never rewrites the binary
+in place).
+
+## Tier-1 targets
+
+| OS | Arch | Artifact |
+|----|------|----------|
+| macOS | arm64 | `hive-macos-arm64.tar.gz` |
+| Linux (glibc, Ubuntu 22.04+/Arch) | x86_64 | `hive-linux-x86_64-glibc.tar.gz` |
+
+macOS x86_64, Debian/Fedora/WSL2 are tier-2 best-effort and not guaranteed.
+
+## Releasing
+
+Bump `version`, every `url`, and every `sha256` in `hive.rb` together. The
+checksums come from the `SHA256SUMS` file the U1 release workflow publishes.
