+# hive-skills
+
+The hive skills/slash-commands, distributed as a **separate package** via each
+agent's native marketplace (plan: install/packaging U10). The core `hive`
+binary never installs these — they are optional agent-facing wrappers over the
+hive CLI, reached through the marketplace, and removed from the marketplace
+(not by `hive uninstall`).
+
+## Install / remove per agent
+
+### Claude Code
+
+```bash
+claude marketplace add ivankuznetsov/hive-skills
+# then install the skills from the marketplace UI, or:
+claude plugin install hive-skills@hive-skills
+# remove:
+claude plugin uninstall hive-skills
+```
+
+### Codex
+
+```bash
+codex plugin marketplace add ivankuznetsov/hive-skills
+codex plugin install hive-skills@hive-skills
+# remove:
+codex plugin uninstall hive-skills
+```
+
+### Pi
+
+```bash
+# Pi marketplace equivalent (see Pi's marketplace docs); skills live under
+# skills/ and are surfaced as /skill:<name>.
+```
+
+## Contents
+
+| Skill | What it wraps |
+|-------|---------------|
+| `hive-status` | `hive status --json` — summarize tasks across projects |
+| `hive-new` | `hive new <project> "<text>"` — capture a task |
+| `hive-drive` | drive a task through one stage via `hive <verb> <slug> --json` |
+
+Each skill is a plain markdown instruction the agent reads to know which hive
+CLI verb to run and how to parse its `--json` envelope; the heavy lifting stays
+in the hive binary.
