+---
+title: hive uninstall
+type: command
+source: lib/hive/commands/uninstall.rb, lib/hive/service.rb
+created: 2026-08-13
+updated: 2026-08-13
+tags: [command, install, uninstall, cleanup]
+---
+
+**TLDR**: `hive uninstall [--purge]` removes hive cleanly: the daemon service
+registration, the installed binary (per channel), the global config +
+install-channel record, and each registered project's `.hive-state/`
+directory. Completed work is preserved — `.hive-state/stages/8-done/` is left
+in place. Interactive mode prompts before deleting anything and per project;
+`--purge` is the non-interactive CI path. The skills package is **not** touched.
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+hive uninstall            # interactive; prompts before deleting
+hive uninstall --purge    # non-interactive; preserves completed work
+hive uninstall --json     # hive-uninstall.v1 envelope
+```
+
+## Removal order
+
+1. Snapshot registered projects (before deleting the global config).
+2. `Hive::Service.remove!` — stop + disable + delete the launchd/systemd unit.
+3. Remove the binary (bash: delete `~/.local/bin/hive`/`hv`; brew: `brew
+   uninstall hive`; aur: `yay -R hive-bin`).
+4. Delete `~/.config/hive/config.yml` + the install-channel record.
+5. Per project: remove `.hive-state/` except `stages/8-done/`.
+
+## Completed-work preservation
+
+`8-done` (merged, archived tasks) is never destroyed — the marker directory and
+its artifacts survive even under `--purge`. See [[modules/config]] for the
+registry, [[commands/init]] for the daemon-service registration it reverses.
+
+## Backlinks
+
+- [[commands/update]] — forward lifecycle verb
+- [[commands/init]] — registers the service `uninstall` removes
+- [[cli]] — command table entry
