index 000000000..ee4963d59
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wiki/commands/update.md
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+---
+title: hive update
+type: command
+source: lib/hive/commands/update.rb, lib/hive/install.rb
+created: 2026-08-13
+updated: 2026-08-13
+tags: [command, install, update, packaging]
+---
+
+**TLDR**: `hive update` updates hive via the package manager that installed it. It reads the install channel recorded at install time (`~/.config/hive/install-channel`) and shells out to `brew upgrade hive`, `yay -Syu hive-bin`, or re-runs the `install.sh` one-liner. Hive never rewrites its own binary in place (R-UPD). Unknown/unrecorded channel exits 1.
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+hive update          # text output
+hive update --json   # hive-update.v1 envelope (channel + command)
+```
+
+## Channel → command
+
+| Channel | Command |
+|---------|---------|
+| `brew` | `brew upgrade hive` |
+| `aur` | `yay -Syu hive-bin` |
+| `bash` | `curl -fsSL <release>/install.sh \| bash` |
+
+The channel is recorded by each installer (`install.sh`, the tap formula, the
+PKGBUILD) into `~/.config/hive/install-channel`. See [[modules/config]].
+
+## Why shell out
+
+In-place binary self-update is explicitly rejected (R-UPD). The native package
+manager is the source of truth for the binary, so `hive update` delegates to it
+and never mutates its own executable.
+
+## Backlinks
+
+- [[commands/uninstall]] — inverse lifecycle verb
+- [[cli]] — command table entry
